{"chunk_id": "2f5548b63664", "text": "This section recounts the origin of Sikhandin and the vow that will one day bring about Bhishma\u2019s fall. After the wronged princess Amba performs severe austerities, the god Siva appears and promises that she will be the cause of Bhishma\u2019s death, even granting that she will gain manhood in another birth and remember her former life. Filled with wrath, Amba immolates herself to fulfill that destiny. Later, King Drupada, desiring a son who will destroy Bhishma, also worships Siva. The god foretells that the child will first be female and later male. When Drupada\u2019s queen gives birth to a daughter, the couple secretly raises her as a son and names her Sikhandin. Only a few know the truth. The child is trained as a warrior and even married as a man, setting the stage for the prophecy that will ultimately lead to Bhishma\u2019s downfall.\nAmba gains Shiva\u2019s promise to destroy Bhishma, self\u2011immolates, and is reborn as Drupada\u2019s child Sikhandin, secretly raised as a son.\nThemes: vengeance and destiny, divine prophecy, rebirth, gender transformation, deception in royal lineage", "vector": [-0.0031654841732233763, -0.029392825439572334, -0.003864835249260068, 0.015231801196932793, -0.025163257494568825, 0.03560333326458931, -0.04339323192834854, -0.012213548645377159, -0.016101807355880737, -0.004728149157017469, 0.023998787626624107, 0.011517544277012348, 0.03605841100215912, 0.013398095965385437, 0.006772663909941912, 0.014361795037984848, 0.04521355405449867, 0.0027840198017656803, 0.0014338372275233269, -0.022285543382167816, -0.007073819637298584, 0.006685663014650345, 0.024386944249272346, 0.0330066978931427, -0.03645995259284973, 0.01465625874698162, 0.015258570201694965, -0.019287368282675743, 0.009516529738903046, -0.01187893096357584, -0.02105415053665638, -0.002069610869511962, -0.0010649210307747126, -0.0085193682461977, -0.037396881729364395, 0.008432367816567421, -0.021817078813910484, -0.014522